OL,3,GNEWSAWorld War Two artwork saved from
OL,4,Aleaky roof
OL,5,
OL,6,FRare artworks from World War Two at
OL,7,Frisk of being washed away have been
OL,8,Fsaved by repairs to a leaky roof.
OL,10,FThe paintings, two murals of military
OL,11,Finsignia, are at RAF Bungay, a former
OL,12,Fairfield near Flixton, Suffolk, where
OL,13,Fabout 3,000 United States Army Air
OL,14,FForces (USAAF) personnel were based.
OL,16,FThe USAAF Heritage Trust, a charity
OL,17,Fdedicated to preserving the site, was
OL,18,Frecently granted a 125-year lease and
OL,19,Fit appealed for help to fix the roof.
OL,20,FThe plea came after two irreplaceable
OL,21,Fpieces of art had already been lost.
OL,23,APub: 09-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,380,370,200,160,0,100
